  "text": "Subscribe to skip adsAdvertisementZoologyA Rope Bridge Camera Just Discovered a New Species of Howler MonkeyThese monkeys can now travel further afieldDNBy David Nield7:00 AM CST on November 20, 2026Add Nautilus to GoogleCamera traps are important devices for conservationists and photographers, providing a non-invasive way in which they can keep tabs on the behaviors and movements of wildlife over time. Occasionally, camera traps also help to identify a new species too.Powered By 10 ShareNextStayCase in point: A camera trap embedded in the Alta Floresta region of the Amazon rainforest, toward the western edge of Brazil, snapped a photo of a new howler monkey species, Alouatta matogrossensis, not long after the species was first described in a study in Communications Biology.Read more: “Qatari Sand Cats Caught on Camera for the First Time”Subscribe to skip adsAdvertisement",
